-->

<statement>
<p>
	This function returns true if the player clicked on a valid location of the figure.
</p>

<tabular valign="top" top="minor">
	<col width="12%"/>
	<col width="88%"/>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell>Inputs:</cell>
		<cell>
			<p><pf>state</pf> (1 x 1) number — struct object representing the current game state.</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell>Outputs:</cell>
		<cell>
			<p><pf>true</pf> (1 x 1) number — result (1 x 1) <pf>true</pf> if the click is valid. <pf>false</pf>, otherwise. See below for definition of valid.</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell>Details:</cell>
		<cell><p>I recommend assuming the click is valid and thinking about what would make it invalid.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>Play the demo again to refresh your memory.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>Clicks on the reset or new game button will always be considered valid.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>This function does not change the state structure in any way.</p></cell>
	</row>
</tabular>

</statement>
